-Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`; contract: `skill://ipc-contract`. The only crate that knows both `merge-core` and `gitio`; owns decode (UTF-8, EOL, binary), captured stages (`stages.rs`), opening (`open.rs`), finish/save/take/reset (`writes.rs`), and describe/take for files the editor cannot show (`sides.rs`, plan §2 #36). A text file deleted on one side loads with `FileMergeData.deleted` and base as the deleted side's text (plan §2 #47). The disk is the truth (plan §2 #52/#53): each file remembers what yamt last saw on disk and which view that selects (`disk.rs` `Seen`: `GitOutput`, `ViewFromStages`, `ViewFromDisk`); finish and save record the bytes they wrote (`Seen::after_own_write`: the view stays, `GitOutput` becomes `ViewFromStages`), take reads the file back (a failed read-back is a warning, the next look settles it); a path unreadable at `open` starts as `GitOutput`. Each file also keeps what this run found at open (`disk.rs` `AtOpen`: `Untouched`, `Changed`, `Unread`; set once in `open.rs`, never written again). Save (plan §2 #65, #69) is finish without `git add`: it skips bytes already on disk, never changes `DiskVersion` or `settled`, and never comes back as a `DiskChange`. Reset (plan §2 #66) puts the captured stages back and then the file from `AtOpen`: a regular file's bytes (a link there is removed first) or its absence; a link, submodule, other entry or `Unread` → `checkout -m` where git can, then read back; a folder or submodule at the path is `NotAFile` before the index is touched; afterwards `Untouched` selects the stages view, `Changed` the disk view. `waiting.rs` tells the window what each chunk looks like on disk while a side waits (`Waiting`: `SideLines`, `Markers` from `MarkerStyle` — the first block of the file at open, else `ours`/`theirs` merge style — or from an exactly located block's own lines, `AsShown` for an inexact block or raw region). `refresh` settles every difference in `disk.rs` (no marker lines → one batched `git add